 \n• Iron-rich foods (Spinach\, chickpeas and beef. Baby draws on your ir
 on\, so ask your doctor about supplements too.)\n\nWeek 28\, month 7 of th
 e guide.
CATEGORIES:Food
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ummi-20260928@ummi.local
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Sūrah al-Anʿām (6) after Fajr
DESCRIPTION:For forty days\, on Mondays.\n\nAlso today:\n• Ṣalawāt 140
  times\n• Sūrah al-Mulk (67) and Sūrah an-Nūr (24) (Often\, from this
  month onward.)\n• The five sūrahs after your prayers (After the daily 
 prayers and the tasbīḥ of Sayyidah Fāṭimah (as): al-Ḥashr (59)\, a
 ṣ-Ṣaff (61)\, al-Jumuʿah (62)\, at-Taghābun (64) and al-Qadr (97).)\
 n• Sūrah al-Ikhlāṣ (112) in the daily prayers\n• Sūrah Yāsīn (3
 6) over almonds (Then eat them on an empty stomach.)\n• Melon after your
  food (No water just before or after it. Watermelon and kharbozeh are name
 d in particular. Mustadrak al-Wasāʾil\, Vol. 3\, p.635.)\n• Iron-rich 
 foods (Spinach\, chickpeas and beef. Baby draws on your iron\, so ask your
  doctor about supplements too.)\n\nWeek 28\, month 7 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Sūrah
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
